### Variables
@base = http://localhost:8080
@notificationBase = http://localhost:8081
@k8sBase = http://192.168.49.2

### Create offer (Docker local)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/offers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Ivan Petrov",
  "customerEmail": "ivan@example.com",
  "customerTelegram": "@ivan",
  "title": "Need Java developer",
  "description": "Need help with Spring Boot project"
}

### List offers
GET {{base}}/api/v1/offers?page=0&size=20
Accept: application/json

### Get notifications (after 5 seconds)
GET {{notificationBase}}/api/v1/notifications
Accept: application/json

### Get events (after 5 seconds)
GET {{notificationBase}}/api/v1/events
Accept: application/json

### Create offer (via K8s Ingress)
POST http://192.168.49.2/api/v1/offers
Host: offers-notification.local
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "K8s Client",
  "customerEmail": "k8s-client@example.com",
  "customerTelegram": "@k8sclient",
  "title": "Test K8s Ingress",
  "description": "Via Ingress"
}

### Get notifications via K8s Ingress (after 5 seconds)
GET http://192.168.49.2/api/v1/notifications
Host: offers-notification.local
Accept: application/json

### Duplicate event (idempotency test) - replace ID
POST {{notificationBase}}/internal/api/v1/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "REPLACE-WITH-REAL-EVENT-ID",
  "eventType": "OfferCreated",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-18T12:00:00Z",
  "source": "offers-service",
  "payload": {
    "offerId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "customerName": "Test",
    "customerEmail": "test@example.com",
    "title": "Test",
    "description": "Test"
  }
}